## What landed

**Rust core** (`src/rustcore/src/session.rs`, +`lib.rs`, +`rustcore.h`):
- Session store owns the schema: versioned `ARSS`-v1 binary over a JSON manifest — per-window opaque shell blob + structured tab records (`url`, `container`, `group`, `engine`, `state`) + group definitions
- Every field bounds-checked on decode; atomic temp+fsync+rename into `<data-dir>/session.dat` (0600)
- Engine-state blob stays opaque — WebEngine `serializePageHistory` today, a future engine can carry its own bytes under its own tag
- `rc_session_save/load/exists/clear/encode/decode` FFI, panic-safe, `RcStatus`/`RcBuffer` conventions

**Qt side**:
- `TabWidget` gained a shared `TabSessionSnapshot` — the legacy stream path and the JSON manifest serialize identical state, plus `sessionStateJson()`/`restoreSessionState()`
- `BrowserApplication`: `saveSession` writes via `rc_session_save` (retires the QSettings blob on success), `restoreLastSession` arms the crash guard only after full-blob validation — `RC_CORRUPT` returns without restoring, `RC_NOT_FOUND` falls back to the legacy reader once; `canRestoreSession`/`clearPrivateDataOnExit` cover both stores
- `--session-smoke`/`--restore-smoke` exercise the Rust codec

## Verification

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| cargo test | 51/51 (9 session tests) |
| `--session-smoke` | 8/8 PASS through Rust path |
| `--restore-smoke` | PASS (urls, index, titles) |
| Legacy 0xec/v2 session | restored once via fallback |
| Corrupted `session.dat` | clean exit, `restoring=false` — no crash-prompt loop |
| `make check` | rc=0, 63 programs, 0 failed |
| No-rust | check-warnings clean-copy build+link PASS |

Notes on two findings along the way: the earlier "no-rust link failure" turned out to be `OBJECTS_DIR` pointing into the source tree so the shadow build reused Rust objects — the clean-copy build proves sources are correct; and I tightened the manifest version check to reject non-u64 values (`"version": -1`) that would have slipped through.

