## Summary

**Rust core** (`src/rustcore/src/tlsprobe.rs` + FFI): `rc_tls_check(host, port, flags)` performs a real blocking TLS 1.2/1.3 handshake (SNI=host, ALPN `http/1.1`, 5s/5s/15s timeouts) and evaluates the chain with rustls+webpki against platform roots (rustls-native-certs) plus `rc_tls_add_root` anchors. A `CaptureVerifier` records the actually-evaluated chain so rejected chains return summarized. Verdicts are honest: `verified` / `warning` (expired, not-yet-valid, bad-hostname, untrusted-root, broken-chain, weak-signature, revoked) / `unverified` (network, protocol, root-store — never a false alarm) / `refused` (private-host SSRF discipline, invalid input); `"revocation":"not-checked"` — no OCSP/CRL fetch.

