## What landed

**Build system (the task core)**
- New root `.qmake.conf` auto-adds `CONFIG+=rustcore rustdl adblock_rust` when a cargo toolchain resolves (PATH first, then `~/.cargo/bin` — fixed `$$HOME` → `$$(HOME)` env expansion).
- `arora.pro` warns loudly and falls back to Qt paths when cargo is absent.
- Opt-outs: `CONFIG+=no-rust` (all crates) or per-crate `CONFIG-=rustcore/-rustdl/-adblock_rust`.
- `adblock.pri` gained its missing cargo make target — fresh default builds now link `libarora_adblock_ffi.a`.
- `check-warnings.sh` pinned to `CONFIG+=no-rust` so the fallback build stays gated.
- README, `src/rustcore/README.md`, `.devin/qt-env.sh`, ChangeLog all document rust-as-default.

**Adblock parity fixes** (uncovered by testing under the new default)
- `AdBlockRule::setEnabled` was eating the first filter char on unchanged state (`||x^` → `|x^`), silently corrupting the rule text fed to the Rust engine — now a no-op when state doesn't change.
- `AdBlockNetwork::match()` is rust-primary but gates on document-level unbreak first (`$document`/`$genericblock` — the crate leaves page-scope exceptions to the embedder), falls back to the native matcher on rust allows, and prefers the native `removeParams` representation for `$removeparam` rewrites.
- Rust `data:` redirect stubs map back to canonical `arora-resource:` names so Chromium can serve them.
- `--autofill-smoke` now probes `autofill-store.dat` under rustcore.

## Verified

- Configure matrix: cargo on PATH / only `~/.cargo/bin` / no cargo / `no-rust` / per-crate opt-out — all correct.
- Fresh `qmake && make` links all three archives; `--adblock-rust-smoke` 13/13 + native agrees; `--autofill-smoke` PASS.
- `make check` rc=0: check-warnings PASS, supply-chain PASS, **69 test programs, 0 failures** — the differential test asserts strict composite≡linear parity on the whole corpus.

