## What was wrong

New tabs were blank "Untitled" because `newTab()` only created the tab — nothing ever navigated it. The start page itself was never broken: `qrc:/startpage.html` loads fine and `tst_WebPage::webChannelStartPage` was already green. No Servo backend exists in this tree, so the WebEngine path was the whole story.

## Fix

Split tab creation into two roles:

- **`newTab()`/`makeNewTab()`** — unchanged, bare programmatic tabs (window ctor, session restore, link/context spawns, `loadUrl` tab branches, second-instance). The `startupBehavior` preference stays authoritative at launch.
- **`newTabPage()`/`newTabPageInContainer()`** — new user-facing entry points that create the tab, then load `MainWindow/home` (default `about:home` → `qrc:/startpage.html`) via `loadString()`, so a customized home page applies to new tabs too — same target `goHome()` resolves.

Wired every user-facing surface to it: Ctrl+T / File > New Tab action, the tab-strip "+" and empty-strip double-click (`TabBar::newTab`), the "New Container Tab" menu entries, the refill tab when the last tab closes with `quitAsLastTabClosed` off, and the tab recreated when a close is refused.

## Verification

- `tst_tabwidget` 17/17 — new `newTabStartPage` covers default home → `qrc:/startpage.html` + title `Welcome to Arora!` (channel handshake), custom home, and bare `newTab()`
- `tst_webpage` 69/69, `tst_browsermainwindow` 17/17
- `--browser-smoke`, `--tabstrip-smoke` PASS
- `make check` rc=0 (warnings/supplychain/coverage gates + full autotest suite), offscreen with `--disable-gpu`

One note: the first `make check` attempt showed a SIGSEGV in `tst_BrowserMainWindow::chromeSlots` — that was caused by my own concurrent `make` racing the check run in the shared `autotests/.obj` dir; the clean re-run passed 17/17.
