## What landed

**`src/data/extshim.js`** — the gapfill preamble covering the EXT13 27-API delta plus everything real Bitwarden exposed:
- `chrome.runtime` (sendMessage/onMessage, connect/onConnect + External variants, getURL/id/lastError/getManifest/getPlatformInfo, lifecycle events)
- `chrome.storage.local` (persisted per-extension under `<data>/extstorage/<id>/`) + `session` (in-memory) + `onChanged`
- `chrome.extension`, `chrome.i18n`, `chrome.alarms` (host-side `QTimer`s), `chrome.action`/`browserAction`
- Partial-native repair: `installNs`/`fillNs`/`repairInstalls` — Chromium swaps in a reduced `chrome.tabs` late in bootstrap, so every installed surface is re-verified on a schedule
- Typed-error proxies for unsupported namespaces + `shim.audit()` 114-surface checklist

**`ExtensionShimBackend`** — host side of `ChromeBridge::invoke`: storage, alarms, action state, platform info, `{ok:false,error:"typed-code"}` for unsupported calls.

**Relay** — same-extension message fan-out + full Port routing (`portConnect/Accept/Message/Disconnect`), extension-id filtered.

**Merged-code injection** — the fix for the last blocker. Bitwarden's webpack requires `719.background.js` via a *synchronous* `importScripts()` that the MV3 `script-src 'self'` CSP makes impossible in DOM code (eval/inline refused, `<script src>` async, and webpack's patched `push` doesn't replay the pre-patch queue). `extensionCodeSource()` now merges manifest entries + sibling chunks into a second `DocumentReady` MainWorld injection — CSP-exempt, so chunks register through the patched `push` in the same synchronous pass.

## Verified

- `--extension-host-smoke`: **0 failures** on generated fixture **and** real Bitwarden — audit **114/114**, zero unshimmed-API errors; Bitwarden drives alarms, tabs.query, sidePanel, relay, sendMessage; `connectNative` answered a typed "no native messaging host" note
- `tst_extensionmanager` 20/20 incl. `extensionShimBackend` + `extensionMessageRelay`
- Deno-host parses both JS files; build clean
- Suite green except pre-existing unrelated failures (xbel/adblock/sandbox/tabwidget/browsermainwindow/historymanager)

